From cadd222cb3dac95dd182009fbead352c08401202 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarkJiang-maji <chiang142536@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:34:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] Retire the v53 monitor; v71 runs on its own

cgu/monitor now deploys only v71. v53 crash-looped wherever a node has an
untagged image (kubernetes 12.0.1 rejects names: null), was patched by hand
differently on .4 (sitecustomize ConfigMap) and .6 (pip install at start),
and billed at hardcoded rates 2/10. Nothing still needs it: the admin Home
page and the fair scheduler read v71, and v71 exports the legacy metric
names the Grafana dashboards use.

- v71 gets its own ServiceMonitor; it was scraped through v53's.
- v71 resumes cumulative cost from Prometheus, not from v53's prom-app.
- README: how the cost resume works, and the manual cleanup for clusters
  that still run v53 (kubectl apply does not prune).
